From 1515c6b5150d2a0fc5795755920eec653c39814f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakshay <b.lakshay@iitg.ac.in>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:42:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] HBF: attach modes (direct / behind HBM), front-end
 latency, prefetcher + LHB

-gpgpu_hbf_attach 1 gives HBF its own per-sub-partition L2->HBF queue and
credit pool (-gpgpu_hbf_credits) so the tiers cannot head-of-line block each
other; 2 additionally charges every HBM request byte and HBF reply byte of a
partition to one PHY token bucket (-gpgpu_hbf_phy_gbps), as when HBF data
crosses the HBM stack's link (H3). -gpgpu_hbf_frontend_latency_ns delays each
HBF request. New stats: credits, end-to-end read latency avg/p50/p95/p99, PHY.

-gpgpu_hbf_prefetch_file streams per-kernel page hints (hbf-prefetch-v1) into a
latency-hiding buffer (-gpgpu_hbf_lhb_pages, window, lookahead, hit latency).
Prefetch reads yield to demand reads; demand merges into in-flight prefetches;
prefetch-only work does not hold kernel completion.
